[{"id":2561690079,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6YsEnf","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?u=a254c0fcd6cf4668367407a460e175559e12dc6f&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While this is reasonable, I'd like to warn that this is making a certain hole we already have a bit deeper. I mean, to me, it doesn't make much sense that those methods are part of the interface of  `ResourceLoader`. That's already the case in the C++ side of things, but I'd rather avoid extending the damage.\r\n\r\nSomething doable here is making `ResourceLoader` friend of `core_bind::ResourceLoader` so `_validate_local_path()` can be used. In a future Godot versiom, I'd suggest exposing those functions via `Resource` instead.\r\n\r\nLastly, the commit message would ideally be about the why rather than the what. This is entirely optional, but when browsing the repo history it'd be mroe convenient to know right away why these change happened than having to check the PR for context.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101752#pullrequestreview-2561690079","pul